questions.statement:
Let $\hat{i}, \hat{j}$ and $\hat{k}$ be the unit vectors along the three positive coordinate axes. Let
$$
\begin{aligned}
\vec{a} &= 3\hat{i} + \hat{j} - \hat{k} \, , \\
\vec{b} &= \hat{i} + b_2\hat{j} + b_3\hat{k} \, , \qquad b_2, b_3 \in \mathbb{R} \, , \\
\vec{c} &= c_1\hat{i} + c_2\hat{j} + c_3\hat{k} \, , \qquad c_1, c_2, c_3 \in \mathbb{R}
\end{aligned}
$$
be three vectors such that $b_2 b_3 > 0$, $\vec{a} \cdot \vec{b} = 0$ and
$$
\begin{pmatrix}
0 & -c_3 & c_2 \\
c_3 & 0 & -c_1 \\
-c_2 & c_1 & 0
\end{pmatrix}
\begin{pmatrix}
1 \\ b_2 \\ b_3
\end{pmatrix}
=
\begin{pmatrix}
3 - c_1 \\ 1 - c_2 \\ -1 - c_3
\end{pmatrix}.
$$
Then, which of the following is/are TRUE ?
